Title: Zentrum's republican tendencies have faltered...
subtitles: **Weimar Alliance** shatters.
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: ((z_relation < 60 and ideology != "reformist") or (z_relation < 50 and ideology != "reformist")) and z_party_leader == "Ludwig Kaas" and year >= 1930 and year <= 1932 and pro_republic <= 50 and (unemployed > 15)
on-arrival: z_relation *= 0.80; z_ideology = "Authoritarian Catholic Tent"; presidential_patience -= 5 if spd_in_government and president == "Hindenburg"; z_right_labor -= 200; z_left_labor -= 250; z_clerical_wing *= 1.5

​= Zentrum undergoes a shift in priorities.

​Following his election victory, Prelate Ludwig Kaas—a compromise candidate between the party's left and right—has been steadily shifting Zentrum to the right. He has turned the party away from its commitment to the republic and toward vague, Catholic-oriented policies, even displaying authoritarian tendencies and a willingness to dismantle democracy when the time comes.

​With the unofficial **Weimar Divorce**, the SPD [? if ddp_votes > 0: and possibly [+ ddp_name +] ?] remain the sole parties loyal to the republican order. Our time has come.

​@root: Perhaps Zentrum was never committed to democracy to begin with?
